    "data_quality_notes": "High-quality data available for core kinase domain structure and Wnt signaling interactions. Limited quantitative kinetic data available for most protein-protein interactions (only Km ~100 nM for beta-catenin phosphorylation found). Specific residues for autophosphorylation sites and some PTMs not fully mapped. Alternative splice variant sequences incomplete in public databases. Good structural coverage with multiple PDB structures and AlphaFold prediction.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "CSNK1A1 is essential for modeling canonical Wnt signaling as it initiates the beta-catenin phosphorylation cascade in the destruction complex. Its enzymatic activity (Km ~100 nM for beta-catenin) makes it a key control point for beta-catenin stability and downstream transcriptional responses. Also critical for circadian rhythm models involving PER/CRY dynamics. Autophosphorylation-mediated regulation of substrate specificity adds complexity to kinetic modeling."
